<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="path-check"><span aria-hidden="true">01</span>Choose a supported path</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">For an Apple-to-Apple move, Apple’s Quick Start flow is designed for a current Apple device and a nearby new Apple device. The source needs Wi-Fi and Bluetooth available, and the new device follows the prompts shown during setup. See <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.apple.com/en-au/102659">Apple’s Quick Start guidance</a>. For Android, the copy process is used during initial setup, with cable or wireless options that can vary by manufacturer, device version and tablet model. See <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.google.com/android/answer/13761358?hl=en">Google’s Android transfer guidance</a>.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Before choosing a method, write down the exact source and destination models. Check whether the destination is a phone or tablet, whether it is already in use, and whether the manufacturer provides a different process. Apple-to-Android and Android-to-Apple moves need different planning. They are not a standard version of the same household transfer.</p>{% call note("care", "Take care", "A phone guide is not universal") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Some tablets and manufacturer variants need their own instructions. Do not assume that a method shown for one phone will cover another device.</p>{% endcall %}
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="transfer-backup"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span>Know what kind of movement is happening</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">A transfer copies or moves selected content from one device to another during setup. A backup is a stored recovery copy with its own scope. Synchronisation keeps some account-based content available across devices. These are related but different jobs.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">For example, photos already synchronised to an account may not be copied into a backup in the same way as local photos. An app icon appearing on the destination does not prove that its local records, downloads, messages or account session are present. A transfer can finish while separate downloads or account checks are still pending.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Plan to verify representative content rather than treating a completion message as a full inventory. If the new device is already being used, do not reset it simply to return to an initial setup. Assess what is already on that device first and preserve anything that matters.</p>{% call note("care", "Take care", "Completion is not proof of completeness") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Keep the source device available until important records, account access and pending downloads have been checked on the destination.</p>{% endcall %}
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="readiness"><span aria-hidden="true">03</span>Check both devices before starting</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">A supported path assumes a working, unlocked source device, accessible accounts, a usable destination and enough storage. Check power, a compatible cable if one is needed, reliable Wi-Fi and current software compatibility. Keep both devices charged and close by. Direct transfers can occupy both devices until they finish, while an iCloud download may continue in the background; timing varies. The <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.apple.com/en-au/102659">Apple guidance</a> also notes that managed devices may be excluded from the ordinary Quick Start path.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Ask what matters before touching the setup process: contacts, photos, messages, local files, app-specific records and authenticator access. If the source is broken, locked or suspected to be compromised, stop the routine transfer plan. A specialist, device manufacturer or account provider may need to handle the next step.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">These checks are preparation, not permission to erase the source. The source should remain available until the destination has passed a separate verification checklist.</p>{% call note("care", "Take care", "Cross-platform moves need a separate plan") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Banking, myGov, mobile-service activation, authenticator recovery and provider account recovery are not established by Wi-Fi or by a generic copy process.</p>{% endcall %}
